-- the ground state transform on one edge: with φ = u·ψ at its two ends (variables u_x, u_y, ψ_x, ψ_y),
-- (φ_x − φ_y)² = ψ_x ψ_y (u_x − u_y)² + u_x² ψ_x (ψ_x − ψ_y) + u_y² ψ_y (ψ_y − ψ_x). Summed over the edges of a vertex
-- the last two terms are φ² (Lψ)/ψ, so ⟨φ, Lφ⟩ = Σ_edges ψψ(u − u)² + Σ φ² (Lψ)/ψ; with ψ = √G this is the Hardy square.
dz-gst : (A : Type) → (A → A → A) → (A → A → A) → (BQ → A) → List A → A × A
dz-gst A ad mu q vs = (λ g sub → (λ d e → (mu d d , ad (mu (mu (g 2) (g 3)) (mu e e)) (ad (mu (mu (mu (g 0) (g 0)) (g 2)) (sub (g 2) (g 3))) (mu (mu (mu (g 1) (g 1)) (g 3)) (sub (g 3) (g 2)))))) (sub (mu (g 0) (g 2)) (mu (g 1) (g 3))) (sub (g 0) (g 1))) (λ i → al-nth A (q (fn-q 0 1)) i vs) (al-gsub A ad mu q)
